# Shiro v2 environment — copy to .env for local development.
# NO KEYS ARE REQUIRED: with none set, Shiro runs entirely on the built-in
# demo provider (free, offline, seed-pack content only). That is the default
# and the recommended mode for development and demos.
#
# Production providers (founder's paid accounts): Anthropic (Claude) for
# ladder planning + teaching; Google (Gemini) for item generation +
# feedback. Embeddings stay local/open — no key, no third party.
#
# Keys are supplied by the founder through secure entry and dropped into
# env vars — they can live wherever he keeps them. (He believes the paid
# keys were left in the old learn-anything repo; nothing in this codebase
# reads that repo — env vars are the only contract.)
# NEVER commit a filled .env — it is gitignored; this example is the only
# env file that belongs in the repo.
#
# WARNING: EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the client bundle and are
# extractable. The bare names below are preferred; the app also accepts the
# EXPO_PUBLIC_-prefixed variants. Use throwaway keys locally only —
# production must proxy model calls through a backend holding keys
# server-side (see README → Deploy).

# Anthropic (Claude) — frontier jobs: ladder_planning, teaching
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1

# Google (Gemini) — volume jobs: item_generation, feedback
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=            # accepted alias for GEMINI_API_KEY
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# GEMINI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta
